{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class HeightAllTheSame {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n        int l = sc.nextInt();\n        int r = sc.nextInt();\n        sc.close();\n        \n        long total = (long) n * m;\n        final int MOD = 998244353;\n        \n        if (total % 2 == 1) {\n            long base = r - l + 1;\n            System.out.println(power(base, total, MOD));\n        } else {\n            int k = r - l + 1;\n            int evenCount = (r >> 1) - (l >> 1);\n            if ((l & 1) == 0) evenCount++;\n            int oddCount = k - evenCount;\n            \n            long sum = (evenCount + oddCount) % MOD;\n            long diff = ((evenCount - oddCount) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n            long term1 = power(sum, total, MOD);\n            long term2 = power(diff, total, MOD);\n            long inv2 = power(2, MOD - 2, MOD);\n            long ans = ((term1 + term2) % MOD * inv2) % MOD;\n            System.out.println(ans);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static long power(long base, long exp, int mod) {\n        base %= mod;\n        long res = 1;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % mod;\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long power(long long base, long long exp, int mod) {\n    base %= mod;\n    long long res = 1;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m, l, r;\n    cin >> n >> m >> l >> r;\n    \n    long long total = (long long) n * m;\n    const int MOD = 998244353;\n    \n    if (total % 2 == 1) {\n        long long base = r - l + 1;\n        cout << power(base, total, MOD) << endl;\n    } else {\n        int k = r - l + 1;\n        int evenCount = (r >> 1) - (l >> 1);\n        if ((l & 1) == 0) evenCount++;\n        int oddCount = k - evenCount;\n        \n        long long sum = (evenCount + oddCount) % MOD;\n        long long diff = ((evenCount - oddCount) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n        long long term1 = power(sum, total, MOD);\n        long long term2 = power(diff, total, MOD);\n        long long inv2 = power(2, MOD - 2, MOD);\n        long long ans = ((term1 + term2) % MOD * inv2) % MOD;\n        cout << ans << endl;\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00015245705435518175, -2.145764938177308e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00016664070426486433, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.168244216387393e-05, -0.0011709030950441957, -0.01820240542292595, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.000